  "title": "Altan Khan",
  "summary": "Altan Khan (1507-1582) led the Tumed Mongols and ruled from 1543. He raided Ming China every year from 1550 to 1566 and besieged Beijing in October 1550. A 1571 settlement gave trade markets and him the title shunyiwang. In 1578 he gave Sonam Gyatso the title that became Dalai Lama, and in 1581 he built Hongci (Dazhao) Monastery at Hohhot.",
